      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Fix Homebrew cask updater detection",
        "body": "Fixes #10\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\nFixes Homebrew cask install detection so Sparkle stays disabled when Nameplate is installed through Homebrew but the app bundle lives at `/Applications/Nameplate.app`.\r\n\r\nModern Homebrew casks can place the app directly in `/Applications`, so checking only whether the bundle path contains `/Caskroom/` can miss Homebrew-managed installs. This keeps the existing legacy Caskroom path detection and also checks the standard Homebrew cask receipt locations:\r\n\r\n- `/opt/homebrew/Caskroom/nameplate`\r\n- `/usr/local/Caskroom/nameplate`\r\n\r\n## Validation\r\n\r\n- `git diff --check`\r\n- `swift build`\r\n\r\nFocused behavior proof:\r\n\r\n```text\r\nPROOF modern-app-with-receipt=true\r\nPROOF modern-app-without-receipt=false\r\nPROOF old-caskroom-path=true\r\n```",
        "branch": "fix/issue-10-homebrew-receipt-updater",
